                     default=0,
                     description="Add a delay to LedFx's output to sync with your audio. Useful for Bluetooth devices which typically have a short audio lag.",
                 ): vol.All(vol.Coerce(int), vol.Range(min=0, max=5000)),
+                # Android-only: "System Audio (root)" (REMOTE_SUBMIX) is an
+                # exclusive tap on some ROMs, silencing the phone's own
+                # speaker unless LedFx echoes the captured audio back out
+                # through a second AudioTrack. Auto-detection can get this
+                # wrong (e.g. before a permission it needs is granted, it
+                # fails safe and assumes echo IS needed) - this override lets
+                # the user correct it without waiting on a new build. Inert
+                # on every other platform and every other Android input.
+                vol.Optional(
+                    "android_remote_submix_echo",
+                    default="auto",
+                    description='Only affects the Android "System Audio (root)" input. Auto detects whether the ROM already plays audio through the speaker while capturing and only echoes it back when needed; On/Off override that detection.',
+                ): vol.In(["auto", "on", "off"]),
             },
             extra=vol.ALLOW_EXTRA,
         )
